1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,302
A dialer profile has four modes, and they differ in three things:

2
00:00:05,302 --> 00:00:10,332
who presses Dial, whether an agent is held before the customer's phone rings,

3
00:00:10,332 --> 00:00:12,029
and what can go wrong.

4
00:00:12,029 --> 00:00:16,513
This video explains how each one works, what every mode shows in the

5
00:00:16,513 --> 00:00:19,240
profile form, and when to choose which.

6
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,474
For every mode, ask three questions.

7
00:00:26,474 --> 00:00:28,104
Who starts the call:

8
00:00:28,104 --> 00:00:29,985
an agent, or the system?

9
00:00:29,985 --> 00:00:34,374
Is an agent held for the call before the customer's phone rings?

10
00:00:34,374 --> 00:00:36,130
And what can go wrong?

11
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,869
Two things are not modes.

12
00:00:38,869 --> 00:00:40,730
Manual dialing is gone:

13
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:45,670
an older profile saved as Manual is shown, and saved again, as Preview.

14
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,761
And an A.I.

15
00:00:46,761 --> 00:00:50,868
voice agent calling a contact is not a dialer mode either.

16
00:00:50,868 --> 00:00:52,600
It has its own video.

17
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,492
In Preview, the agent is in control.

18
00:00:59,492 --> 00:01:03,402
A record is offered to an agent who is signed in to the

19
00:01:03,402 --> 00:01:05,517
campaign, with a countdown.

20
00:01:05,517 --> 00:01:10,260
The agent reads the record, then clicks Dial, or Skip to pass it on.

21
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:14,721
The agent is held by the offer, before any call exists.

22
00:01:14,721 --> 00:01:20,318
When the agent clicks Dial, the server runs the compliance checks and places the call.

23
00:01:20,318 --> 00:01:23,420
The agent is on the call from the first ring.

24
00:01:24,997 --> 00:01:30,459
Open Interaction Center, Management, Dialer Profiles, and click Add Dialer Profile.

25
00:01:30,459 --> 00:01:32,423
Preview is the first Mode.

26
00:01:32,423 --> 00:01:34,203
Notice what is missing.

27
00:01:34,203 --> 00:01:39,051
There is no Calls per agent, no ring time, no answering machine screening

28
00:01:39,051 --> 00:01:41,137
and no Abandoned calls card.

29
00:01:41,137 --> 00:01:45,617
The agent places the call and listens to it, so none of them apply.

30
00:01:47,217 --> 00:01:50,920
What can go wrong is slow work, not abandoned calls.

31
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:56,155
If nobody responds, the offer runs out and the record goes to another agent.

32
00:01:56,155 --> 00:02:01,071
If the call ends before it connects, the dialer records the outcome and

33
00:02:01,071 --> 00:02:03,177
the agent returns to Ready.

34
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,794
In Power, nobody presses anything.

35
00:02:09,794 --> 00:02:14,689
When an agent in the campaign is available, the dialer reserves that agent,

36
00:02:14,689 --> 00:02:16,502
then calls the customer.

37
00:02:16,502 --> 00:02:21,094
Each call has its own reserved agent, so it never rings more customers

38
00:02:21,094 --> 00:02:22,907
than it has free agents.

39
00:02:23,657 --> 00:02:29,604
While it rings, the agent is Reserved, and the screen says waiting for a connected call.

40
00:02:29,604 --> 00:02:34,917
When a person answers, the agent is joined, and the activity opens on its own.

41
00:02:36,522 --> 00:02:38,798
Choose Power, and the form grows.

42
00:02:38,798 --> 00:02:42,882
Calls per agent is the most calls the dialer may start each time

43
00:02:42,882 --> 00:02:45,799
it looks at the campaign, from one to three.

44
00:02:45,799 --> 00:02:48,542
Each of them reserves a free agent first.

45
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:54,947
Power adds ring time, answering machine screening, and Show each dial to the agent.

46
00:02:54,947 --> 00:02:57,845
It also adds the Abandoned calls card.

47
00:02:59,445 --> 00:03:02,250
What can go wrong is an abandoned call.

48
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:07,299
A person answers, and no agent is connected within two seconds, for example

49
00:03:07,299 --> 00:03:09,980
because the agent's phone was closed.

50
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:13,845
The person hears the abandoned call message, or silence.

51
00:03:14,595 --> 00:03:18,965
A voicemail, a busy line or no answer never reaches the agent.

52
00:03:18,965 --> 00:03:24,815
The dialer records the outcome itself, and the agent goes straight back to Available.

53
00:03:29,016 --> 00:03:30,504
Choose Progressive.

54
00:03:30,504 --> 00:03:34,790
It reserves an agent for every call, just like Power, but the form

55
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:36,516
has no Calls per agent.

56
00:03:36,516 --> 00:03:39,372
The dialer does not ration calls per look.

57
00:03:39,372 --> 00:03:43,598
It keeps going until every free agent holds a call, with a safety

58
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:46,276
limit of one hundred calls in one look.

59
00:03:46,757 --> 00:03:48,610
So the two behave alike.

60
00:03:48,610 --> 00:03:53,368
Power with one call per agent fills the free agents one call at a time.

61
00:03:53,368 --> 00:03:55,902
Progressive fills them all at once.

62
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,694
The risks are the same:

63
00:03:57,694 --> 00:04:01,587
abandoned calls, and the cap on the Abandoned calls card.

64
00:04:05,776 --> 00:04:09,543
Choose Predictive, and a Predictive pacing card appears.

65
00:04:09,543 --> 00:04:12,641
Pacing starts as One call per reserved agent.

66
00:04:12,641 --> 00:04:16,894
Every call still reserves a free agent, so it cannot call ahead.

67
00:04:16,894 --> 00:04:19,203
What Predictive adds is a brake:

68
00:04:19,203 --> 00:04:23,577
with the cap on, it places fewer calls per look as the abandonment

69
00:04:23,577 --> 00:04:25,096
rate nears the cap.

70
00:04:25,613 --> 00:04:30,617
Pick Over-dial, and the dialer places more calls than there are free agents,

71
00:04:30,617 --> 00:04:33,179
because most calls are not answered.

72
00:04:33,179 --> 00:04:36,108
No agent is reserved while the calls ring.

73
00:04:36,108 --> 00:04:39,463
When a person answers, a free agent is connected.

74
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,778
The settings steer it.

75
00:04:41,778 --> 00:04:47,048
Target abandonment rate is what over-dialing aims for, and it must stay below

76
00:04:47,048 --> 00:04:49,271
the Maximum abandonment rate.

77
00:04:49,271 --> 00:04:53,970
Lines per agent and Calls in flight cap how many calls ring at once.

78
00:04:55,570 --> 00:04:58,604
What can go wrong is the whole point of the cap.

79
00:04:58,604 --> 00:05:02,762
When a person answers and nobody is free, the call is abandoned, and

80
00:05:02,762 --> 00:05:05,571
the person hears the abandoned call message.

81
00:05:05,571 --> 00:05:09,729
Over-dialing needs the cap and the message, and it falls back to one

82
00:05:09,729 --> 00:05:13,550
call per reserved agent until its measurements can be trusted.

83
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:19,397
Who presses Dial?

84
00:05:19,397 --> 00:05:21,401
In Preview, the agent.

85
00:05:21,401 --> 00:05:25,053
In Power, Progressive and Predictive, nobody.

86
00:05:25,053 --> 00:05:26,700
The system dials.

87
00:05:27,450 --> 00:05:31,043
Is an agent held before the customer's phone rings?

88
00:05:31,043 --> 00:05:33,817
Yes in Preview, Power and Progressive.

89
00:05:33,817 --> 00:05:38,230
In Predictive, yes by default, and no when you choose Over-dial.

90
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:40,955
Can a call be abandoned?

91
00:05:40,955 --> 00:05:42,469
Never in Preview.

92
00:05:42,469 --> 00:05:47,340
In Power and Progressive, when an agent cannot be connected in time.

93
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:52,540
In Predictive, the same, and on purpose in Over-dial when nobody is free.

94
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:54,744
Which features?

95
00:05:54,744 --> 00:05:58,554
Contact Center Outbound Dialer gives you Preview.

96
00:05:58,554 --> 00:06:03,680
Contact Center Paced Dialing adds Power, Progressive and Predictive.

97
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,451
Start with Preview.

98
00:06:09,451 --> 00:06:13,598
Agents read each record before the call, and a new team or a

99
00:06:13,598 --> 00:06:15,672
high value list needs that.

100
00:06:15,672 --> 00:06:17,620
No call can be abandoned.

101
00:06:18,370 --> 00:06:23,610
Move to Progressive or Power when the list is steady and agents wait between calls.

102
00:06:23,610 --> 00:06:28,380
Turn on the abandonment cap, and the abandoned call message, before you do.

103
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:33,528
Choose Predictive with one call per reserved agent when you want the brake.

104
00:06:33,528 --> 00:06:39,230
Choose Over-dial only when you have measured the answer rate, and your rules allow abandoned calls.

105
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:45,690
Use one profile for each campaign when its abandonment rate must be measured on its own.

106
00:06:47,690 --> 00:06:49,968
Preview lets the agent decide.

107
00:06:49,968 --> 00:06:53,384
Power and Progressive dial for every free agent.

108
00:06:53,384 --> 00:06:56,295
Predictive adds a brake, or calls ahead.

109
00:06:56,295 --> 00:06:57,940
Thanks for watching.

